[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2755489285","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104658#issuecomment-2755489285","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104658","id":2755489285,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kPW4F","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T19:07:44Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T19:07:44Z","body":"Can you explain the problem you're trying to solve?\r\n\r\n`OpenXRCompositionLayer` will register itself (via `_setup_composition_layer_provider()`) when it's in the tree and visible, and unregister itself (via `_clear_composition_layer_provider()`) when it's either not visible or not in the tree.\r\n\r\nSo, I don't think we should automatically call `_setup_composition_layer_provider()` in `OpenXRCompositionLayer::set_layer_viewport()`, at least without first checking if the node is visible or in the tree yet, because it might not be.\r\n\r\nHowever, I don't know why you want to make sure it's registered when the viewport is updated? I think it should be fine to do `set_layer_viewport()` and then later (when the node is added to the tree) do the registration.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2755489285/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2755750970","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104658#issuecomment-2755750970","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104658","id":2755750970,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kQWw6","user":{"login":"m4gr3d","id":914968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxNDk2OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/914968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d","html_url":"https://github.com/m4gr3d","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/m4gr3d/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T21:07:58Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T21:10:45Z","body":"> Can you explain the problem you're trying to solve?\r\n> \r\n> `OpenXRCompositionLayer` will register itself (via `_setup_composition_layer_provider()`) when it's in the tree and visible, and unregister itself (via `_clear_composition_layer_provider()`) when it's either not visible or not in the tree.\r\n> \r\n> So, I don't think we should automatically call `_setup_composition_layer_provider()` in `OpenXRCompositionLayer::set_layer_viewport()`, at least without first checking if the node is visible or in the tree yet, because it might not be.\r\n> \r\n> However, I don't know why you want to make sure it's registered when the viewport is updated? I think it should be fine to do `set_layer_viewport()` and then later (when the node is added to the tree) do the registration.\r\n\r\n@dsnopek `_setup_composition_layer_provider()` doesn't perform the registration when `layer_viewport == nullptr && use_android_surface == false`, so it's possible that while visible in the tree, the node may not register itself if that condition is met.\r\n\r\nThe fix ensures that when we update the `layer_viewport` (e.g: from `nullptr` to a valid value), we perform the registration if it wasn't done already.\r\n\r\nA scenario where that could occur, if creating the node dynamically at runtime, adding it to the tree, then at a later time, using `set_use_android_surface(...)` or `set_layer_viewport(...)` to update those properties.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2755750970/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2755784669","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104658#issuecomment-2755784669","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104658","id":2755784669,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6kQe_d","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T21:27:08Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T21:27:08Z","body":"Ah, ok, that makes sense. But then I think the code should be:\r\n\r\n```\r\n\tif (!registered && is_natively_support() && openxr_session_running && is_inside_tree() && is_visible()) {\r\n\t\t_setup_composition_layer_provider();\r\n\t}\r\n```\r\n\r\n... because we don't want to register the layer unless all those things are true","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2755784669/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2761880834","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104658#issuecomment-2761880834","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104658","id":2761880834,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6knvUC","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a